================================================================================
## Paged completion review fixes — emitted-key continuations, duplicate-page
## stall, discarded-work errors (PR #206 review, issue #173)
================================================================================

Context: maintainer review of PR #206 (the paged Stage-3 completion fix for
issue #173). Three orchestrator defects had to be addressed before merge:
(1) `_queue_next_page` re-injected each page's raw JSON into the message
history — worst case 16 x ~8k completion tokens on top of the schema
prompt, dying on the INPUT cap the same way the single-shot answer died on
the output cap; (2) a `has_more` page contributing zero new items ended the
substage as success, silently dropping items the model still claimed to
have; (3) a ghost-ref/malformed page deep in the run discarded up to 16 LLM
calls of paid work with no indication in the error.

Changes:

1. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py`
   `build_continuation_user_prompt` now takes `emitted_keys` (sequence of
   compact per-item key strings) and embeds them via the new
   `_emitted_keys_block` helper (capped at 400 keys, beyond which dedupe is
   the backstop) so the model knows exactly what NOT to re-emit — instead
   of the previous "none of the N already emitted" with no list.
   `build_truncated_page_retry_prompt` docstring notes the truncated blob
   is no longer re-injected either.
2. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py`
   - `_queue_next_page` / `_queue_truncation_retry` no longer append the
     assistant page payload — the continuation is a single user message
     carrying the emitted-key list; history stays O(keys) not O(pages).
   - `_run_completion` takes a `label_fn` per substage formatting emitted
     keys (`domain --label--> range` for relations, `domain.label` for
     attributes, `subject --kind--> object` for axioms).
   - Duplicate-page handling: a `has_more` page adding zero NEW items is
     tolerated once; `_MAX_DUPLICATE_PAGES` (2) consecutive duplicates fail
     the substage with a "stalled" error instead of a silent early success.
   - `_gathered_note` appends "(<N> <items> gathered over <P> accepted
     page(s) are not checkpointed — the whole substage must be re-run)" to
     every mid-substage failure (truncation, rejection, stall, budget), so
     discarded paid work is visible in the user-facing error while pages
     intentionally stay un-checkpointed.
   - Extracted `_completion_call` (LLM call + usage/step bookkeeping) and
     `_continuation_error` (dup-stall vs page-budget reason) to keep
     `_run_completion` at 119 LOC = the shrink-only baseline.
3. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_staged.py`
   `test_continuation_lists_emitted_keys_not_raw_pages` (key list present,
   no assistant turn echoes raw page JSON),
   `test_single_duplicate_page_is_tolerated_then_paging_continues`,
   `test_duplicate_page_streak_fails_instead_of_silent_data_loss`,
   `test_rejection_error_reports_discarded_pages`; the old
   zero-new-items-stops-paging test was replaced by the stall semantics.
4. `tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl`
   `staged-paged-attributes-repeat-stops-003` replaced by
   `staged-paged-attributes-repeat-stalled-003` (3 duplicate `has_more`
   pages -> failure) + new `staged-paged-attributes-repeat-tolerated-011`
   (one dup page tolerated, next page still delivers); 42 staged rows >=
   the 41 floor.
5. Local SPEC.md (gitignored `.planning/` since upstream 6cf90c3e)
   §3a paged-completion paragraph updated (emitted-key continuations,
   dup-streak, `_gathered_note` discarded-work reporting); §5 contract row
   and §6 failure-mode row updated for 11 `paged_completion` rows and the
   new stall semantics.

