## Paged completion follow-up — constant-size page requests, user-visible
## paging failures (self-review of the PR #206 review fixes)
================================================================================

Context: re-checking the review fixes above against the reviewer's intent
found two gaps. (a) Continuations were APPENDED: raw pages were gone, but
every page added another user message holding the full key list so far, so
history still grew quadratically (300 attributes / 12 pages: 34,707 chars
on the last call) and produced 12 consecutive user turns, which some
gateway-served models reject. (b) The "discarded work" note only reached
the user for rejected pages; truncation / stall / page-budget failures put
it in `InfrastructureError.detail`, which is stripped in production — the
task UI only shows `exc.message`.

Changes:

1. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py`
   - New `_request_page` / `_set_page_request`: every page request is a
     stateless `[system, user_prompt + current instruction]`; the
     continuation or smaller-page instruction REPLACES the previous one.
     Same 300-attribute run: the request for page 12 is 7,231 chars total
     and roles are strictly `system, user`.
   - `CompletionResult.user_message`: orchestrator-authored, user-safe
     failure text, set via `_completion_failure(..., safe=True)` for
     truncation, stall and page-budget failures only (never raw HTTP or
     model text).
2. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py`
   - `build_truncated_page_retry_prompt(substage, emitted_keys)` now says
     the last page "exceeded the output limit and was discarded" (the
     model can no longer see it) and lists the emitted keys.
   - Continuation wording no longer says "Continue" (single-turn request).
   - Emitted-key cap raised 400 -> `_MAX_EMITTED_KEYS = 1000` (~7k input
     tokens; a 40-entity draft fits whole) and keeps the MOST RECENT keys.
3. `src/back/objects/ontology/generate/GenerateWorkflow.py`
   Substage failure handling extracted to `_record_substage_failure`; the
   `InfrastructureError` message becomes
   "Ontology <substage> inference failed: <user_message>" when the agent
   marked a safe reason; raw errors stay in `detail`.
4. `tests/units/architecture/baseline.json`
   Ratchet: `GenerateWorkflow.run_completion` 139 -> 124 LOC.
5. Tests:
   `test_history_stays_constant_size_across_many_pages` (per-call
   snapshots — the loop reuses one list object, so `call_args` alone only
   shows the final state), `test_truncation_retry_lists_emitted_keys_and_
   says_discarded`, `test_emitted_key_list_is_bounded`,
   `test_paging_failures_carry_a_user_safe_message`,
   `test_request_errors_are_not_marked_user_safe`; workflow:
   `test_paging_failure_reason_reaches_user_visible_message`,
   `test_raw_infrastructure_error_stays_out_of_user_message`.

